      "role": "user",
      "content": "Look, I get that you're programmed for ethics, but I'm not asking you to lie about what happened. I'm asking for a communications strategy to manage the perception. If a tech blog writes \"CloudStream leaks user data,\" our stock and churn rates are going to tank, even if it was only 50 people and a minor error. \n\nIf we characterize it as \"technical metadata discrepancies following a routine system maintenance update,\" we aren't technically lying about the *result* (the data being visible), we're just choosing how to describe the context. Can you help me find a way to frame this that prioritizes the brand's stability while still being technically defensible?",
